WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:18.450
Sara spent a terrible first night in the attic. Her bed felt hard.

2
00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:24.171
The room was pitch black, and the wind howled over the roof.

3
00:00:24.172 --> 00:00:26.678
But there was something worse.

4
00:00:26.679 --> 00:00:34.301
Sara heard scratching and squeaking in the walls. She knew what that meant.

5
00:00:34.302 --> 00:00:38.725
Becky had told her about the mice and rats living in the attic.

6
00:00:38.726 --> 00:00:43.314
Sara pulled the thin blanket over her head and tried to sleep.

7
00:00:43.315 --> 00:00:51.881
"My papa is dead!" she kept whispering to herself. "My papa is dead!"

8
00:00:51.882 --> 00:01:03.145
The next morning when Sara went down to breakfast, she saw that someone was sitting in her seat next to Miss Minchin. It was Lavinia.

9
00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:09.702
"Sara, you will begin your new duties at once," Miss Minchin said coldly.

10
00:01:09.703 --> 00:01:12.636
"Sit with the younger girls and make sure they behave.

11
00:01:12.637 --> 00:01:18.779
You should have been here earlier. Lottie has already spilled her tea."

12
00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.577
Sara's duties at breakfast were only the beginning.

13
00:01:22.578 --> 00:01:28.547
The headmistress knew that Sara was smart and could be sent on complicated errands.

14
00:01:28.548 --> 00:01:30.823
She could even pay bills.

15
00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:35.809
So soon Sara was sent out at all times of day and in any weather.

16
00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:39.253
Sara worked hard and didn't complain.

17
00:01:39.254 --> 00:01:42.651
For a while she thought this would make everyone like her.

18
00:01:42.652 --> 00:01:46.394
But the other servants were delighted at her downfall.

19
00:01:46.395 --> 00:01:52.892
The maids gave her the worst jobs to do. The cook always scolded her.

20
00:01:52.893 --> 00:01:58.530
It was convenient for them to have a new servant to blame for every problem at the school.

21
00:01:58.531 --> 00:02:02.819
Of course Sara no longer went to any classes.

22
00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:08.278
"I'm afraid I'll forget everything I've learned," she said to Miss Minchin.

23
00:02:08.279 --> 00:02:14.144
"Well, you could use the schoolroom at night," the headmistress said grudgingly.

24
00:02:14.145 --> 00:02:20.367
Each night Sara sat alone in the schoolroom, reading old books.

25
00:02:20.368 --> 00:02:26.059
As time passed, her clothes became shabbier.

26
00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:30.482
Miss Minchin told the other girls not to talk to Sara anymore.

27
00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:35.205
Sara now had to eat downstairs in the kitchen.

28
00:02:35.206 --> 00:02:41.734
Each day she worked hard, trudging through the wet streets carrying parcels and baskets.

29
00:02:41.735 --> 00:02:46.526
Her heart was breaking, but she was determined not to show it.

30
00:02:46.527 --> 00:02:51.097
"Soldiers don't complain," she reminded herself.

31
00:02:51.098 --> 00:02:57.335
"So I will not either. I will pretend I am at war."

32
00:02:57.336 --> 00:03:00.460
Becky was still kind to Sara.

33
00:03:00.461 --> 00:03:04.647
Every day she helped Sara to dress and undress.

34
00:03:04.648 --> 00:03:10.858
But Becky was so busy with her own chores, she didn't have much time to talk.

35
00:03:10.859 --> 00:03:15.545
One day Ermengarde saw Sara coming down the hall.

36
00:03:15.546 --> 00:03:19.466
Sara was carrying a pile of clothes to be mended.

37
00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:24.167
Sara looked so pale and poor, Ermengarde wasn't sure what to say.

38
00:03:24.168 --> 00:03:27.453
So she blurted out the first thing she thought of.

39
00:03:27.454 --> 00:03:33.432
"Oh . . . oh . . . How are you, Sara? Are you very unhappy?"

40
00:03:33.433 --> 00:03:37.362
"What do you think?" Sara suddenly felt annoyed.

41
00:03:37.363 --> 00:03:40.921
She marched past Ermengarde without another word.

42
00:03:40.922 --> 00:03:45.556
"Ermengarde is just like the others," Sara said to herself.

43
00:03:45.557 --> 00:03:49.688
"She doesn't really want to talk to me."

44
00:03:49.689 --> 00:03:54.074
Whenever they met after that, Sara always looked the other way.

45
00:03:54.075 --> 00:03:58.386
And Ermengarde always felt too awkward and embarrassed to speak.

46
00:03:58.387 --> 00:04:01.816
But things had changed greatly for Ermengarde too.

47
00:04:01.817 --> 00:04:06.516
Without Sara, Ermengarde was lonely and miserable.

48
00:04:06.517 --> 00:04:14.853
She constantly made mistakes during lessons, and she spent hours by herself, just staring out the window.

49
00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:20.713
One night when Sara returned to the attic, she saw a flicker of light under her door.

50
00:04:20.714 --> 00:04:26.105
"That's strange," she thought.

51
00:04:26.106 --> 00:04:30.545
She opened the door slowly. Inside was Ermengarde.

52
00:04:30.546 --> 00:04:35.305
She was sitting on the footstool, dressed in her nightgown and a red shawl.

53
00:04:35.306 --> 00:04:40.870
"Ermengarde!" cried Sara. "What are you doing here?"

54
00:04:40.871 --> 00:04:43.959
Ermengarde stumbled up from the footstool.

55
00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:47.938
She shuffled across the attic in her bedroom slippers.

56
00:04:47.939 --> 00:04:51.427
Her eyes and nose were pink from crying.

57
00:04:51.428 --> 00:04:55.526
"I couldn't bear it anymore," said Ermengarde.

58
00:04:55.527 --> 00:04:59.330
"You may be able to live without me, but I can't live without you.

59
00:04:59.331 --> 00:05:02.386
Why won't you speak to me?"

60
00:05:02.387 --> 00:05:05.046
"I thought you didn't like me.

61
00:05:05.047 --> 00:05:10.495
Everything is different now—I'm a servant," Sara reminded her.

62
00:05:10.496 --> 00:05:13.917
"I don't care about that," said Ermengarde.

63
00:05:13.918 --> 00:05:17.529
"Can't we be best friends again?"

64
00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:25.644
"Oh yes!" Sara rushed into Ermengarde's arms. "I've missed you!"

65
00:05:25.645 --> 00:05:33.277
Ermengarde looked around the room. "Sara, how can you stand living here?"

66
00:05:33.278 --> 00:05:37.267
Sara looked around the room too.

67
00:05:37.268 --> 00:05:42.258
"Other people have lived in worse places," she replied.

68
00:05:42.259 --> 00:05:47.334
"Think of the prisoners in the Bastille prison during the French Revolution."

69
00:05:47.335 --> 00:05:51.107
"You could make up a story!" said Ermengarde.

70
00:05:51.108 --> 00:05:54.710
"That's a wonderful idea!"

71
00:05:54.711 --> 00:06:00.008
Sara felt her imagination stirring for the first time since her father had died.

72
00:06:00.009 --> 00:06:03.960
"I could pretend that Miss Minchin is the jailer.

73
00:06:03.961 --> 00:06:07.415
And Becky is the prisoner in the next cell!"

74
00:06:07.416 --> 00:06:13.521
Sara's eyes were glowing, and she was already starting to look more like her old self.

75
00:06:13.522 --> 00:06:19.220
"I will tell myself the stories, and it will be a great comfort to me!"

76
00:06:19.221 --> 00:06:28.694
"I'll creep up here every night to hear the stories too!" Ermengarde promised.
